# Ada Coding Standards (Host)

Applies to `compiler/`, `jit/`, `common/`, `lir/`, `lovelace/`, `tooling/`, `hypatia/`, `alexandria/`, `format/`, and host test crates. Native Augusta Ada has extra ZFP constraints (see Augusta rules).

## Toolchain

- Ada via GNAT + Alire. Use Ada 2022 (`-gnat2022`) unless the user specifies otherwise.
- Every crate has a `.gpr` and `alire.toml`. Compiler switches live in the `.gpr`, not ad-hoc command lines.
- Host library crates (`compiler`, `lir`, `common`, `jit`, `tooling`, `hypatia`, `alexandria`, `format`): `for Library_Kind use "static";`. **`lovelace`** is an executable, not a library. **`augusta`** native backing is the only `Library_Kind use "dynamic"` crate.

## Warnings as errors (mandatory)

Host Ada **must** treat warnings as errors. This is not optional and must not be turned off in `.gpr` files or command lines.

GNAT default switches for Ada **must** include at least:

- `-gnatwae` — enable all warnings **and** treat them as errors (`-gnatwe` is required; `-gnatwa` alone is not enough)
- `-gnaty` with a full style set (identifiers, keywords, pragmas, layout, no tabs, no trailing blanks, end labels)
- a max line length style check (do not exceed it)
- `-gnato` overflow checks
- `-fstack-check`

Do not add `pragma Warnings (Off)`, `-gnatwn`, or style exemptions unless the user explicitly allows that instance.

```ada
-- BAD
pragma Warnings (Off);
with Ada.Text_IO;  -- unused

-- GOOD
with Ada.Text_IO;
procedure Report (Msg : String) is
begin
   Ada.Text_IO.Put_Line (Msg);
end Report;
```

## Style

- Package/type/subprogram names: `Mixed_Case`; constants `Mixed_Case`; avoid abbreviations unless domain-standard (`LIR`, `WIT`, `WASM`).
- One public package spec per compilation unit; keep bodies focused.
- No dead `with`s, unused entities, or implicit falling-through conditionals.
- Prefer explicit named associations for calls with more than two parameters.
- Do not use GNAT extensions unless required (ZFP, `System.Machine_Code`, C convention).

## Public Ada documentation

Every subprogram (and type) **visible outside its package** must have a documentation comment on the spec. Bodies do not replace spec docs.

```ada
-- BAD
function Tokenize (Source : String) return Token_List;

-- GOOD
--  Split Source into tokens. Raises Constraint_Error if Source is empty.
function Tokenize (Source : String) return Token_List;
```

## C interop

- Wasmtime, libgit2, and OS APIs: `Interfaces.C`, `pragma Import (C | Stdcall, ...)`, `pragma Convention (C, ...)`, `pragma Export` only at true FFI boundaries.
- Keep FFI types in dedicated binding packages; do not scatter `pragma Import` through compiler logic.